author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Comments, notes and learnings retain literal annotation prefixes across positional, add, file, stdin, add-from-stdin and file-from-stdin transports; Explicit SDK text-prefixed structured input and other commands retain supported option normalization; Disposable source mutation rejects the original prefix-loss defect with a behavior assertion and the recorded historical lineage remains registered; Exact all-source coverage, strict static gates and isolated Node and Bun acceptance pass with unchanged thresholds"
goal: context-management
objective: Preserve trustworthy recursive self-improvement evidence
value: Agents can retain exact evidence text across all supported annotation transports
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Public bootstrap normalization preserves literal annotation evidence across comments, notes and learnings; the touched private normalizer now has a meaningful docstring."
expected_result: "Every positional, flag, file and stdin annotation transport must preserve evidence bytes, and the touched normalizer must retain documented responsibilities."
actual_result: "All18 real annotation transports per runtime pass on Node and Bun. Literal-prefix source controls reject the original defect; the shared six-control linked execution passes. The normalizer docstring describes declared flags, linked-test normalization, literal bodies and transformation recording. Local whole-suite timing failures are disclosed; exact-head hosted complete source coverage is enforced before merge."
